  "modified": "2026-11-10T18:45:46Z",
  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: double free and corruption of a shared GSS-TSIG\n     security context under concurrent use\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-94300.patch: hold a new per-key mutex across\n       gss_get_mic(), gss_verify_mic() and gss_export_sec_context() in\n       lib/dns/gssapi_link.c, and release an empty exported buffer\n       (upstream 1d93eddce0).\n     - CVE-2026-94300\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: cache poisoning via a signed wildcard whose RRSIG\n     Labels field is shorter than its Signer Name\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-11721.patch: reject such RRSIGs when parsing\n       in lib/dns/rdata/generic/rrsig_46.c and when verifying in\n       dns_dnssec_verify3() in lib/dns/dnssec.c; stop dnssec-signzone from\n       signing out-of-zone records; add an RRSIG rdata unit test (upstream\n       06778424f0, e5b16cfd1c, 5f3b7aef42).\n     - CVE-2026-11721\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: assertion failure when a NOQNAME proof cannot be\n     attached or retrieved\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-13204.patch: return an error instead of\n       failing a RUNTIME_CHECK in validated() in lib/dns/resolver.c,\n       addnoqname() in lib/dns/rbtdb.c and query_addnoqnameproof() in\n       bin/named/query.c (upstream 204fde8595; its rdatalist.c part is\n       already provided by CVE-2026-80274.patch).\n     - CVE-2026-13204\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: cache memory exhaustion as expired headers of a\n     continuously referenced name are never reclaimed\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-11622.patch: reference count cache rdataset\n       headers in lib/dns/rbtdb.c so a stale header is freed as soon as\n       nothing uses it rather than when its node is released, including\n       the iterator, additional-cache, DNAME zone cut and NOQNAME proof\n       users (upstream 0b72e907d1, 4b8d5bf6fd, 7fcaccdbd3); stop\n       expire_lru_headers() from reusing a list predecessor that expiry\n       may now free (upstream f88f21b7d8, a prerequisite).  The counter\n       sits in existing structure padding, so the 'map' zone file format\n       and MAPAPI are unchanged.\n     - CVE-2026-11622",
